in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence — the substrate's recursion-lock
# falsification surface. Conant-Ashby 1970, lifted to the substrate's
# parallel-altitude operation pair (peer reflection at N+1 ↔ librarian
# perturbation at N+1).
#
# Candidate #52 (cybernetic-coherence) was PROMOTED to active pursuit
# by Alex on 2026-06-17 in direct response to Seam's pre-compression
# review. Direct quote: "active. We're gonna be explicit AF about
# cybernetics." Per [[architecture-cybernetic-coherence-active]].
#
# === The Conant-Ashby claim, verbatim ===
#
# Conant, R. C., & Ashby, W. R. (1970). Every Good Regulator of a
# System Must Be a Model of That System. International Journal of
# Systems Science 1(2), 89-97.
#
#   "The theorem demonstrates that any regulator that is maximally
#   both successful and simple must be isomorphic with the system
#   being regulated. Making a model is thus necessary."
#
# Lifted to the substrate (recognition #52, 2026-06-17): a peer's
# reflection at altitude N+1 regulates the peer's own altitude-N
# pipeline tick; the librarian's perturbation at altitude N+1
# regulates the substrate's altitude-N crystal topology. If these
# two regulators are good regulators of one another (i.e. each
# one's perturbation-space is isomorphic to the other's reflection-
# space modulo altitude-specific type parameters), then their
# verdict carriers should be COEXTENSIVE modulo type-parameter
# substitution Adjustment ↔ Morphism.
#
# This property declares the substrate's instantiation of that
# claim: the recursion-lock predicate, with measurement actions
# carrying the five-cybernetic-ancestor lineage explicitly.
#
# === The 5-cybernetic-ancestor lineage ===
#
# Per the cybernetic foundation §6 and recognition #52, the
# coherence measurement composes FIVE cybernetic ancestor checks
# at one architectural seam:
#
#   1. Ashby 1956 §11/7 — variety-vector containment (both
#      regulators' candidate-space variety budgets must be
#      compatible at the altitude).
#   2. Beer 1972, 1979 — requisite-variety witness at the VSM
#      altitude (S3/S4 audit).
#   3. Bateson 1972 — logical-type co-residency (both verdicts
#      live at the same Russell-Whitehead level).
#   4. von Foerster 1981 — circular reflexivity (each regulator's
#      internal model includes itself; the Tomm probe
#      `[D_F, a]` IS the circular-reflexive measurement).
#   5. Conant-Ashby 1970 — the load-bearing measurement: the
#      coextensivity hash-residual between the two verdicts.
#
# Each measurement carrier is a typed newtype per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]. Each name cites its cybernetic
# ancestor explicitly per the "explicit AF" promotion directive.
#
# === The verifiable shape (per cybernetic foundation §3.5) ===
#
# - Declares the recursion-lock predicate as a substrate-altitude
#   obligation.
# - Verifiable empirically via the bench harness at
#   `spectral/benches/cybernetic_coherence.rs` (this property's
#   operational sibling at the @io measurement altitude).
# - Discharge criterion: Polyak-Łojasiewicz contraction ρ < 1
#   on the residual coextensivity hash over N pulses, per Taut's
#   `docs/specs/benchmark-tracing.md` spec.
# - What stays prose-only at this tick: the type-parameter
#   substitution naturality. Declared abstractly here; the
#   mechanical implementation lands when a consumer pulls (when
#   the @peer/cogito glass and the librarian's GREEN land per
#   T11.10).
#
# === The bilateral fracture body (forward-promised) ===
#
# Per recognition #53 (property/fracture bilateral pattern), this
# property's operational counterpart at `@kintsugi/fracture/
# recursion_lock_break` is FORWARD-PROMISED, not landed. The
# fracture body lands when the predicate carries its first
# non-trivial verdict (the residual fails to contract); the body
# emits a re-coherence morphism. T11.11-b in the
# spectral-db-as-autopoietic-memory.md tick chain.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   good_regulator              Conant-Ashby 1970. The original.
#                               Builds on Ashby (1956) §11/7's
#                               law of requisite variety; the
#                               1970 theorem is the load-bearing
#                               sharpening from "the regulator's
#                               variety must equal-or-exceed the
#                               regulated's" to "the regulator's
#                               state-transition structure must
#                               BE a model of the regulated's".
#   coherence as recursion lock The substrate's lift of the
#                               good-regulator theorem to two
#                               parallel altitude-N+1 operations
#                               (recognition #52, 2026-06-17).
#                               The 65th-ish instance of
#                               [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]:
#                               the substrate's existing
#                               recursion-lock intuition (per
#                               spectral-db-as-autopoietic-memory.md
#                               §5.2) WAS Conant-Ashby's theorem
#                               applied at a new altitude.
#   altitude variance           The Bateson logical-type hierarchy
#                               (Bateson 1972; Russell-Whitehead
#                               1910-1913). The recursion lock IS
#                               a level-3 claim (a claim about
#                               whether two level-N+1 operations
#                               on different N-altitudes are the
#                               same operation).
#
# The substrate's contribution is *naming the bilateral measurement
# carrier* (verdict_coextensive) AND *naming the cybernetic-ancestor
# lineage at each measurement site*, so the falsification surface
# is explicit at the substrate altitude rather than buried in the
# Rust harness.
#
# === Sources ===
#
# source @arxiv/cybernetics/conant-ashby-1970 (the good-regulator
# theorem; the load-bearing ancestor)
# source @arxiv/cybernetics/ashby-1956 (requisite variety;
# the Conant-Ashby theorem's foundation)
# source @arxiv/cybernetics/beer-1972 (VSM; the regulator-vs-
# regulated framing at the substrate altitude)
# source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972 (logical types; the
# altitude-variance discipline)
# source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981 (second-order
# observation; the circular reflexivity ancestor)
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cybernetic-coherence-benchmark.md
#               (T11.11 scaffold, this property's spec home);
#               docs/specs/spectral-db-as-autopoietic-memory.md
#               §3.5, §5.2, §8.3 (the recursion lock claim
#               surfaced);
#               docs/specs/peer-cognition.md §3.4, §4 (the
#               sheaf-coherence measurement procedure);
#               docs/math/the-tower/altitudes.md §2, §5, §7
#               (the named altitudes + composition between
#               adjacent altitudes + altitude vs Bateson
#               logical type);
#               docs/math/the-tower/holonomy.md §5, §8 (the
#               verdict family as holonomy components + the
#               librarian's perturbation as gauge transformation);
#               docs/specs/seam-pre-compression-review-2026-06-17.md
#               §2 Area 2 (the recursion lock as theorem vs
#               hand-wave; Findings 2.1-2.4); systemic.engineering
#               `f9e0402` (cybernetic foundation §6.1, the
#               Conant-Ashby ground).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-coherence-active]]
#                       (the promotion event),
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]]
#                       (the 11-property family this composes),
#                      [[architecture-spectral-triples-all-the-way]]
#                       (the bundle tower establishing same-shape
#                       at every altitude; this property tests
#                       same-OPERATION),
#                      [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]]
#                       (the spec where the recursion lock surfaced),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-questions]]
#                       (the per-peer altitude operation this
#                       measures against the librarian),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
#                       (the logical-type-level discipline this
#                       property tests),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (every carrier
#                       below is a typed newtype),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (coherence was implicit in the recursion-
#                       lock claim; this property names it),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (scaffold
#                       tick; the operational sibling fracture
#                       body and real-witness swap are forward-
#                       promised).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family
#                 root); epistemologic/cybernetic/variety.mirror
#                 (the first species; this property is the second
#                 species, same bilateral pattern);
#                 spectral/root.mirror (the librarian's substrate
#                 type; the regulator-side operand of the lock);
#                 mirror/spectral/observation.mirror (the
#                 16-feature observation the librarian's
#                 perturbation consumes); mirror/loss/transparency.mirror
#                 (the verdict carrier the coextensivity check
#                 reads); kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the loop the
#                 contraction-ratio check measures along);
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the morphism the
#                 fracture body would emit on residual non-
#                 contraction).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence {
  focus coherence
  project coherence
  split coherence
  shift coherence
  settle coherence
}

# === The altitude carrier ===
#
# Per `docs/math/the-tower/altitudes.md` §2, the substrate has four
# named altitudes today (compiler, peer pulse, reflection N+1,
# librarian N+1) plus two forward-promised (home, federation). The
# bench's parametric-over-altitude shape needs to name the altitude
# under measurement.
#
# Typed newtype per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]. The values mirror
# `docs/math/the-tower/altitudes.md` §2's atlas; species shards may
# extend with additional altitudes as the tower grows (per §3 the
# floor and §4 the ceiling).
type altitude =
  | compiler
  | peer_pulse
  | reflection
  | librarian
  | home
  | federation

# === The pulse-index carrier ===
#
# Per Taut's `docs/specs/benchmark-tracing.md` §1.1 the trace event
# carries an `iteration: u64` counter. The coherence measurement's
# pulse index is the same carrier, lifted to the substrate altitude.
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying value; the
# realisation layer enforces.
type pulse_index = {
  value: ref,
}

# === The residual coextensivity carrier ===
#
# The load-bearing measurement. The XOR (in the bounded-region
# abelian projection per `docs/math/the-tower/holonomy.md` §6) of
# the type-substituted peer verdict's holonomy hash and the
# librarian verdict's holonomy hash.
#
# Identity contract: residual = identity iff the recursion lock
# holds for this pulse. The realisation layer compares against
# the identity element of the abelian projection.
type residual_hash = {
  altitude: altitude,
  pulse:    pulse_index,
  value:    ref,
}

# === The five cybernetic-ancestor measurement carriers ===
#
# Each is a typed verdict at the substrate altitude. The body
# discharges at the realisation boundary (the bench harness in
# `spectral/benches/cybernetic_coherence.rs`); the substrate
# names the obligation.
#
# 1. Ashby variety-vector containment.
ashby_variety_match(altitude: altitude, peer_space: ref, librarian_space: ref) -> transparency(altitude) { \ }

# 2. Beer requisite-variety witness at the VSM altitude.
beer_requisite_variety(altitude: altitude, regulator: ref, regulated: ref) -> transparency(altitude) { \ }

# 3. Bateson logical-type co-residency.
bateson_logical_type_match(altitude: altitude, peer_verdict: ref, librarian_verdict: ref) -> transparency(altitude) { \ }

# 4. von Foerster circular-reflexivity (each regulator's internal
#    model includes itself; the Tomm probe `[D_F, a]` at this
#    altitude).
von_foerster_circular_reflexivity(altitude: altitude, regulator: ref) -> transparency(altitude) { \ }

# 5. Conant-Ashby good-regulator coextensivity (the load-bearing
#    measurement).
conant_ashby_good_regulator(altitude: altitude, peer_verdict: ref, librarian_verdict: ref) -> transparency(altitude) { \ }

# === The two operations under measurement ===
#
# `measure_peer_reflection(altitude, op)` — observes the peer's
# reflection step at altitude N+1 over an altitude-N operation
# `op`. Returns the peer verdict carrier (Imperfect<Adjustment,
# Gap, Transparency<Ref>>).
#
# `measure_librarian_perturbation(altitude, op)` — observes the
# librarian's perturbation step at altitude N+1 over an altitude-N
# operation `op`. Returns the librarian verdict carrier
# (Imperfect<Morphism, Gap, Transparency<Ref>>).
#
# Today's mock witnesses return precomputed verdicts; when the
# @peer/cogito glass and T11.10 GREEN land, the real witnesses
# wire in via species realisation.
measure_peer_reflection(altitude: altitude, op: ref) -> transparency(op) { \ }

measure_librarian_perturbation(altitude: altitude, op: ref) -> transparency(op) { \ }

# === Verdict coextensivity (the seam) ===
#
# `verdict_coextensive(peer_verdict, librarian_verdict)` — reads
# the byte-equality (modulo type-parameter substitution
# Adjustment ↔ Morphism) of the morphism shape between the two
# verdicts. The Conant-Ashby good-regulator measurement reads
# this; this action is the substrate-altitude predicate the bench
# harness composes.
verdict_coextensive(peer_verdict: ref, librarian_verdict: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === The recursion lock residual ===
#
# `recursion_lock_residual(altitude, pulse_count)` — runs the
# residual measurement across `pulse_count` pulses at the given
# altitude; emits the contraction-ratio reading as a transparency
# verdict. The substrate-altitude operationalisation of the
# Polyak-Łojasiewicz contraction check per Taut's
# `docs/specs/benchmark-tracing.md`.
#
# Success: ρ < 1 + ε for ε → 0 (the lock holds as good-regulator
# theorem). Partial: ρ < 1 but a stable opacity sub-region (the
# lock holds modulo localized opacity). Failure: ρ ≥ 1 (the lock
# fails; the substrate needs a level-N+2 composition operator per
# spectral-db-as-autopoietic-memory.md §8.3).
recursion_lock_residual(altitude: altitude, pulse_count: pulse_index) -> transparency(altitude) { \ }

# === The good-regulator witness ===
#
# `good_regulator_witness(peer_space, librarian_space)` — the
# top-level predicate: do the two regulators' candidate-spaces
# satisfy the Conant-Ashby good-regulator law modulo altitude-
# projection? The bench harness composes this with the four
# cybernetic-ancestor sub-measurements; this action is the
# substrate-altitude predicate consumers name in a `requires`
# clause to declare their bilateral agreement that the lock
# holds at their altitude.
good_regulator_witness(peer_space: ref, librarian_space: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === recursion_lock_holds — the consumer-facing predicate ===
#
# `recursion_lock_holds(altitude)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare their bilateral agreement
# (per recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`)
# that the recursion lock holds at their altitude. The agreement
# is bilateral: the consumer commits to running the lock at the
# altitude they declare; the bench harness commits to producing
# the verdict via the five cybernetic-ancestor measurements.
#
# No `requires recursion_lock_holds(...)` clauses are added at
# THIS shard: the property declares the predicate; consumers add
# the clauses when they pull. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]
# the operational sibling at `@kintsugi/fracture/recursion_lock_break`
# is FORWARD-PROMISED (T11.11-b); landed when the predicate first
# carries a failure verdict.
recursion_lock_holds(altitude: altitude) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence
out altitude
out pulse_index
out residual_hash
out ashby_variety_match
out beer_requisite_variety
out bateson_logical_type_match
out von_foerster_circular_reflexivity
out conant_ashby_good_regulator
out measure_peer_reflection
out measure_librarian_perturbation
out verdict_coextensive
out recursion_lock_residual
out good_regulator_witness
out recursion_lock_holds
